Description: Maximum likelihood estimation for parameterized conductance models
  via Newton and quasi-Newton methods, for moderate-sized problems
  such as spatial grids with fewer than a million cells. Supports
  'terra'-native workflows, Gaussian distance and Wishart distance or covariance
  measurement models, spline and scale-aware conductance estimation,
  environmental and diagonal-variance extensions, cross-validation across
  supported conductance models, and selected-pair analysis while retaining all
  focal sites in the resistance graph.
URL: https://github.com/wpeterman/terradish,
  https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21225712
